{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode\/harmonicMinor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Harmonic minor mode, which sharpens the 7th degree."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode\/harmonicminor"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLNumeralV4ModeO13harmonicMinoryA2EmF","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumeral.Mode.harmonicMinor"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/Mode/harmonicMinor":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode\/harmonicMinor","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode\/harmonicminor","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"harmonicMinor","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Harmonic minor mode, which sharpens the 7th degree."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumeral.Mode.harmonicMinor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral/Mode":{"abstract":[{"text":"The numeral-mode type specifies the mode similar to the mode type, but with a restricted set of values. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different minor values are used to interpret numeral-root values of 6 and 7 when present in a minor key. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"harmonic minor value sharpens the 7 and the melodic minor value sharpens both 6 and 7. If a minor mode is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without qualification, either in the mode or numeral-mode elements, natural minor is used.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral\/Mode","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral\/mode","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Mode","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Mode","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNumeral.Mode","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumeral":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumeral","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumeral","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumeral"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The numeral type represents the Roman numeral or Nashville number part of a harmony. It requires that the key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be specified in the encoding, either with a key or numeral-key element."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumeral"}],"title":"MXLNumeral"}}}